WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:38.748
<i>I am a headhunter and I am
the purest form of salesman alive.</i>


00:00:38.788 --> 00:00:40.862
<i>I sell the American dream.</i>


00:00:40.902 --> 00:00:44.262
<i>I make money out of thin air,
smoke, whole cloth.</i>


00:00:44.302 --> 00:00:46.541
<i>I stand on the shoulders of giants,</i>


00:00:46.582 --> 00:00:48.622
<i>the hardest of hardened salesmen.</i>


00:00:48.662 --> 00:00:52.423
<i>Tin men, bible salesmen, slum realtors.</i>


00:00:52.463 --> 00:00:55.543
<i>We're a wolf pack of commissioned
phone jockeys working</i>


00:00:55.583 --> 00:00:58.880
<i>70 hours a week without a net.
You hit, you hit big.</i>


00:00:58.919 --> 00:01:01.223
<i>You blank, and the repo man's tailgating</i>


00:01:01.264 --> 00:01:03.024
<i>the minivan at the grocery store.</i>


00:01:03.064 --> 00:01:07.104
<i>This job is a desk, a phone,
a chair and your ass.</i>


00:01:08.623 --> 00:01:11.104
Good morning,
Imperial Automotive Manufacturing,


00:01:11.145 --> 00:01:12.385
Dottie speaking.


00:01:12.425 --> 00:01:14.353
<i>I am who I say I am.</i>


00:01:14.393 --> 00:01:15.306
Johnny Cobra calling, Dot.


00:01:15.307 --> 00:01:17.186
Need the name of your
Plant Manager, please.


00:01:17.225 --> 00:01:19.745
<i>I'm sorry, but it's
against company policy</i>


00:01:19.786 --> 00:01:22.426
to give out names of employees.
Nature of your business, sir?


00:01:22.466 --> 00:01:24.306
The nature of
my business, Dottie, is that


00:01:24.346 --> 00:01:25.841
I'm down here at the Nissan plant with


00:01:25.842 --> 00:01:28.426
a shut-down line costing me
ninety grand a minute


00:01:28.466 --> 00:01:31.147
because your Quality Department
thinks they can run a freightliner


00:01:31.187 --> 00:01:34.227
full of injection molded crap
down my goddamn throat!


00:01:34.266 --> 00:01:37.227
The person that you need to
speak to is Mr. Rayburn, I'll...


00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:39.188
First name, first name, first name.


00:01:39.227 --> 00:01:40.748
Thomas is his first name.


00:01:40.788 --> 00:01:42.388
- Dottie.
- What?


00:01:42.428 --> 00:01:44.508
Relax. Take a deep breath.
Pat yourself on the back,


00:01:44.548 --> 00:01:46.948
you're doing one helluva job.
- Well, thank you,


00:01:46.988 --> 00:01:49.949
uh, Mr... did you say "Cobra"?


00:01:50.948 --> 00:01:52.029
Call me Johnny.


00:01:52.069 --> 00:01:55.069
Dot, tell me, what's the story on Tom?
Big guy, small guy,


00:01:55.109 --> 00:01:58.428
young, old, play sports, college boy,
what am I dealing with?


00:01:58.469 --> 00:02:00.670
I know Tommy does play golf a lot.


00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:03.238
He's been working here
a couple three years, probably...


00:02:03.278 --> 00:02:06.029
Oh, chitchat's over, Dot.
Boss is on my ass.


00:02:06.031 --> 00:02:07.398
Go on patch me through.


00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:11.511
Rayburn.
- Tom.


00:02:11.551 --> 00:02:14.391
Dane Jensen, Blackridge Recruiting.
Thanks for taking my call.


00:02:14.431 --> 00:02:16.669
Yeah, hold up, hold up, bud.
Lemme save us both some time.


00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:19.112
I'm not lookin' to make
a move right just yet.


00:02:19.152 --> 00:02:21.391
Rough as things are out there,
I'm just happy to have the job I got.


00:02:21.392 --> 00:02:23.632
Now I'm up to my ass in alligators
so if you'll excuse me...


00:02:23.671 --> 00:02:26.352
- Sweet. Baby. Jesus.


00:02:26.391 --> 00:02:29.272
I cannot believe my guy
was wrong about you.


00:02:29.313 --> 00:02:32.953
Scuse me? Your guy? What guy?
- This isn't a random call, Tom.


00:02:32.992 --> 00:02:35.312
I was told by a confidential source


00:02:35.353 --> 00:02:38.873
that even if your golf game was more
screwed up than a soup sandwich,


00:02:38.914 --> 00:02:41.674
you're one of the premier
Plant Managers in the South.


00:02:41.714 --> 00:02:44.714
He also told me even though
you've only been at Imperial


00:02:44.754 --> 00:02:46.514
for three years,
that you were bright enough


00:02:46.553 --> 00:02:48.313
to at least listen to
what I was recruiting for


00:02:48.314 --> 00:02:51.995
before making up your mind.


00:02:53.355 --> 00:02:57.195
So. You're a headhunter, huh?


00:02:57.235 --> 00:03:00.796
<i>I am a headhunter.
And a headhunter cometh.</i>


00:03:00.835 --> 00:03:03.876
What's the deal with this gut, son?


00:03:03.916 --> 00:03:06.916
You need to get some exercise,
buddy, you're starting to look like


00:03:06.956 --> 00:03:08.717
the kind of kid Willy Wonka'd kick out


00:03:08.757 --> 00:03:10.117
of the chocolate factory.


00:03:10.156 --> 00:03:11.597
Hands up.


00:03:11.637 --> 00:03:13.637
I dunno, we could play a little football
when you get home tonight.


00:03:13.677 --> 00:03:15.916
- If it's still light out


00:03:15.957 --> 00:03:19.238
and I don't have
any calls to make, we'll see.


00:03:26.998 --> 00:03:29.599
Good morning.
- Hey, hon.


00:03:29.638 --> 00:03:31.239
Ryan eat breakfast?


00:03:31.278 --> 00:03:34.119
If you can call it that.
- He likes cereal and it's easy.


00:03:34.158 --> 00:03:37.399
Of course he does, Elise,
what kid doesn't like


00:03:37.438 --> 00:03:39.078
colored marshmallows
swimming in whole milk?


00:03:39.079 --> 00:03:41.080
It's a Momma.


00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:46.880
I like your hair, Lauren,


00:03:46.919 --> 00:03:49.361
looks good on you.


00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:52.321
The point is, he's a mess.
- Shh! Be quiet, he'll hear you!


00:03:52.361 --> 00:03:54.921
Anyway, I made an appointment
for him to see the doctor.


00:03:54.961 --> 00:03:56.800
What the hell for, his weight?


00:03:56.841 --> 00:04:00.475
No! I told you a week ago, he's tired
all the time and those bruises...


00:04:00.515 --> 00:04:03.150
Bruises?
- Mom, can I have chocolate milk?


00:04:03.162 --> 00:04:06.562
- Sure you can, baby.
- Yeah, just a sec.


00:04:09.779 --> 00:04:12.432
- Who's calling you so early?
- Just some candidate.


00:04:12.442 --> 00:04:14.963
Pushing sixty and wonders
why he can't find a job.


00:04:15.003 --> 00:04:17.923
Because of his age?
That's awful.


00:04:17.964 --> 00:04:18.844
Okay.


00:04:21.185 --> 00:04:22.404
Gotta go.


00:04:22.443 --> 00:04:24.363
I was thinking maybe
I could drive into the city,


00:04:24.395 --> 00:04:25.708
we could get lunch.


00:04:25.748 --> 00:04:30.356
First of the month, hon, swamped.
Call me! Oh.


00:04:37.589 --> 00:04:41.342
I'm done talking about it!
Either manage Bob to get a deal


00:04:41.573 --> 00:04:43.693
or make the son of a bitch
quit so I don't have to pay


00:04:43.725 --> 00:04:45.605
unemployment on his lazy ass.


00:04:45.645 --> 00:04:47.806
Ed, how do you propose
I force the man to quit?


00:04:47.846 --> 00:04:49.247
For Christ sake, Wilson,


00:04:49.287 --> 00:04:52.407
have a little fun for a change.


00:04:52.447 --> 00:04:55.447
You know what I love about this place?


00:04:55.486 --> 00:04:56.767
I'm on pins and needles.


00:04:56.807 --> 00:04:59.767
Ed only cares about making money.


00:04:59.808 --> 00:05:01.927
Man, woman, black, white, old or young,


00:05:01.967 --> 00:05:05.448
doesn't matter as long as
you're a producer.


00:05:05.487 --> 00:05:07.567
Bob, were you not here
this past Saturday or Sunday?


00:05:07.609 --> 00:05:10.409
No, I don't think anyone was here.


00:05:10.448 --> 00:05:13.529
- You blanked for three months.
- I got two kids,


00:05:13.569 --> 00:05:14.929
my wife had divorced me,


00:05:14.968 --> 00:05:16.608
I started coming in on the weekends.


00:05:16.648 --> 00:05:19.690
Ah, wife and two kids, I see.
You're gonna score in October?


00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:21.890
I'm sure gonna try my best.


00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:25.409
Try? Your attitude is to try?
Bob...


00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:26.768
You know what I hate about this place?


00:05:26.769 --> 00:05:27.932
Nope.


00:05:27.972 --> 00:05:30.531
Ed only cares about making money.


00:05:30.571 --> 00:05:31.930
That's why he tolerates you
and your mouthbreathers.


00:05:31.931 --> 00:05:34.610
My mouthbreathers make more placements


00:05:34.651 --> 00:05:37.532
and out-produce those Ivy Leaguers
you coddle every month.


00:05:37.572 --> 00:05:40.732
What about an attitude that says
"I'll do whatever it takes,


00:05:40.771 --> 00:05:43.052
"I'll work whatever hours necessary,


00:05:43.091 --> 00:05:48.253
in order to justify your
financial commitment to me, Ed"?


00:05:50.612 --> 00:05:53.252
Oh...


00:05:53.293 --> 00:05:56.692
Bob...


00:05:56.733 --> 00:06:00.174
Are you going to get a deal?!


00:06:00.213 --> 00:06:03.253
Yes! Yes, sir.


00:06:03.294 --> 00:06:06.894
Attaboy, Bob. Now get
the fuck back on the phone.


00:06:14.695 --> 00:06:17.896
Bet the place is full this weekend.


00:06:17.935 --> 00:06:21.976
But... if and when Bob leaves,


00:06:22.016 --> 00:06:23.855
then keep your ears open.


00:06:23.896 --> 00:06:25.775
If he breaches his non-compete


00:06:25.816 --> 00:06:28.056
and calls just one of our clients,


00:06:28.096 --> 00:06:29.736
I will sue him so deep and hard,


00:06:29.777 --> 00:06:31.857
that he, his wide-assed
Junior League wife,


00:06:31.896 --> 00:06:34.776
and their two brats will be
sleeping in a cardboard box


00:06:34.816 --> 00:06:37.137
under the overpass on Whacker.


00:06:37.178 --> 00:06:40.338
There's always someone
that thinks they can hang up


00:06:40.378 --> 00:06:43.057
their own shingle, and skip on
down to the home office


00:06:43.098 --> 00:06:46.098
in their skivvies and make
phone calls while the rug rats frolic


00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:49.299
at their feet. It makes me
want to puke blood.


00:06:49.338 --> 00:06:51.499
In 35 years,


00:06:51.538 --> 00:06:54.298
I have never let anyone
slide on their non-compete.


00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:01.100
I leave for Prague in two days.


00:07:01.139 --> 00:07:02.499
Prague?


00:07:02.539 --> 00:07:05.019
You want her to tell you where it is?


00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:09.380
I know where Prague is.
Overseas.


00:07:09.421 --> 00:07:12.940
I want to spend more time
away from the place, travel,


00:07:12.981 --> 00:07:16.581
indulge my inner Kerouac.


00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:19.261
Time to finalize that succession
plan that we dance around


00:07:19.302 --> 00:07:20.662
and never do anything about.


00:07:20.702 --> 00:07:23.381
I won't give up control immediately,


00:07:23.422 --> 00:07:25.782
but one of you will get the job.


00:07:25.821 --> 00:07:29.982
Whoever takes this last quarter
can move into the empty office


00:07:30.023 --> 00:07:32.623
next to this one.
You'll get off a desk


00:07:32.662 --> 00:07:33.942
and you'll receive overrides


00:07:33.983 --> 00:07:35.982
from every recruiter at Blackridge.


00:07:36.022 --> 00:07:40.024
I'll announce the new General Manager
the first of the year. Understood?


00:07:40.063 --> 00:07:42.384
- One hundred percent, Ed.
- Understood.


00:07:42.423 --> 00:07:46.263
Wilson, beat it.


00:08:02.025 --> 00:08:04.426
- The hell is that?
- Cobra wine.


00:08:04.466 --> 00:08:08.506
Spotted it in a small village in Vietnam
last month, thought of you.


00:08:08.547 --> 00:08:10.705
- You're supposed to drink it?
- Don't be such an American.


00:08:10.706 --> 00:08:12.226
Of course you drink it.


00:08:12.267 --> 00:08:15.466
But I'm determined to save it
for a special occasion.


00:08:15.506 --> 00:08:18.188
Maybe the next time I do
something truly remarkable.


00:08:18.227 --> 00:08:19.507
Such as?


00:08:19.548 --> 00:08:21.748
I haven't settled on that as yet.


00:08:21.787 --> 00:08:24.387
How about a record-breaking October?


00:08:24.427 --> 00:08:26.267
What makes a person remarkable
is the life they live,


00:08:26.268 --> 00:08:27.629
not the money they make.


00:08:27.668 --> 00:08:29.508
Spoken like a man with a lot of money.


00:08:31.349 --> 00:08:34.069
I may never uncork that wine.


00:08:35.067 --> 00:08:36.629
Ryan...


00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:39.069
Ryan, wake up, pal.


00:08:39.109 --> 00:08:42.349
- What time is it?
- 6:30. Come on.


00:08:42.389 --> 00:08:45.109
Let's get some roadwork in
before school.


00:08:45.149 --> 00:08:46.590
Roadwork?


00:08:51.231 --> 00:08:53.990
Dad! I need to rest.


00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:56.592
Why don't I just carry you?


00:08:56.631 --> 00:09:00.111
- I'm walking.
- You're jogging.


00:09:00.152 --> 00:09:02.079
Morning, ladies!


00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:08.113
Alright.


00:09:08.152 --> 00:09:10.872
Let's just walk.


00:09:10.912 --> 00:09:13.632
Why don't we go to Catholic school?


00:09:15.472 --> 00:09:18.273
We're lapsed Catholics.


00:09:18.313 --> 00:09:19.594
The good Lord wants us to spend


00:09:19.634 --> 00:09:21.554
Sunday mornings at Cracker Barrel.


00:09:21.593 --> 00:09:23.874
I'm with the Lord.


00:09:25.713 --> 00:09:27.594
How come Lauren doesn't have to jog?


00:09:27.634 --> 00:09:29.954
'Cause Lauren doesn't have
to lose weight.


00:09:31.794 --> 00:09:34.314
First step in solving a problem
is recognizing it, buddy.


00:09:34.354 --> 00:09:36.715
Did you and Grandpa go jogging
when you were a kid in St. Louis?


00:09:36.756 --> 00:09:39.955
- No, not hardly.


00:09:39.995 --> 00:09:41.355
He went to work when it was dark,


00:09:41.395 --> 00:09:42.474
came home when it was dark.


00:09:42.475 --> 00:09:44.675
Wasn't much fun, was he?


00:09:44.716 --> 00:09:47.276
Eh, he did the job.


00:09:48.947 --> 00:09:51.516
"Kinfe," "Sizhong," "Deepak",


00:09:51.557 --> 00:09:54.116
don't get me going on the red dots.


00:09:54.156 --> 00:09:55.635
Here's an invoice begging to be sent.


00:09:55.636 --> 00:09:58.797
"Ping."
Interview a Chinese engineer yet?


00:09:58.838 --> 00:10:01.197
Treat yourself. It's like having
a conversation in the dark


00:10:01.237 --> 00:10:02.997
with Astro from the Jetsons.


00:10:03.037 --> 00:10:05.637
Look, Sumner,


00:10:05.677 --> 00:10:07.117
I should have spent
more time with you, okay.


00:10:07.118 --> 00:10:08.398
My fault. Let's start over.


00:10:08.439 --> 00:10:11.319
We are the "Dixie Mafia."
Okay, Dixie.


00:10:11.358 --> 00:10:13.519
The South. You know,
state's rights, NASCAR,


00:10:13.558 --> 00:10:15.638
closeted atheists, poor spellers.


00:10:15.678 --> 00:10:16.999
I'm not an idiot, Mr. Jensen.


00:10:17.039 --> 00:10:19.759
Okay. Role-play with me, alright.


00:10:19.799 --> 00:10:21.799
I'm a client from
Hattiesburg, Mississippi and


00:10:21.839 --> 00:10:23.319
I'm looking for a process engineer.


00:10:23.359 --> 00:10:27.241
So go on, pitch me one of your PhD's.


00:10:27.280 --> 00:10:30.040
Ahem! Ring! Ring!


00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:33.240
- Darrel Waltrip here!
- Uh, yes, Mr. Waltrip?


00:10:33.281 --> 00:10:35.800
Darrel, son.
What can I do you for?


00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:37.280
Well, Darrel, I'm calling about your...


00:10:37.281 --> 00:10:39.681
Who the hell is this?


00:10:39.722 --> 00:10:40.961
Sumner, Sumner Firestone
from Blackridge Recruiting.


00:10:40.962 --> 00:10:42.202
Spit it out, I'm a busy man!


00:10:42.241 --> 00:10:45.561
Uh... well, I've got a guy, he's uh,


00:10:45.601 --> 00:10:47.842
for your open engineering
position I mean,


00:10:47.882 --> 00:10:50.122
he's got two degrees in
Mechanical Engineering,


00:10:50.162 --> 00:10:51.642
experience reducing waste in the plants.


00:10:51.643 --> 00:10:53.242
Sounds stronger than puppy's breath.


00:10:53.282 --> 00:10:54.201
Now, when can he get down here?


00:10:54.202 --> 00:10:58.083
- Well, he can be there Friday?
- You asking me or telling me?


00:10:58.123 --> 00:10:59.683
I'm telling you.
He'll be there Friday.


00:10:59.723 --> 00:11:02.163
Friday it is! By the by,


00:11:02.204 --> 00:11:05.003
he wouldn't happen to have
one of those PhD's, would he?


00:11:05.043 --> 00:11:06.404
As a matter of fact, he does.


00:11:06.444 --> 00:11:09.044
Perfect!
Better'n a new set of snow tires!


00:11:09.085 --> 00:11:11.604
Now, what's his name?


00:11:11.644 --> 00:11:14.764
Mohammed Al Far...


00:11:14.804 --> 00:11:17.805
Your sleeper-cell starter kits


00:11:17.846 --> 00:11:21.925
are unemployable south of the grit-line!


00:11:26.726 --> 00:11:30.286
Alright. Cowboy up, sunshine.


00:11:30.327 --> 00:11:33.231
Use this guy. Lou Wheeler.


00:11:33.271 --> 00:11:36.247
Bachelor's in Mechanical Engineering,
Six Sigma experience,


00:11:36.287 --> 00:11:38.008
and an age-vague voice.


00:11:38.047 --> 00:11:40.647
-"Age-vague"?
- Yeah. He's 59,


00:11:40.687 --> 00:11:43.167
sounds like he's 39, and
refuses to change the dates


00:11:43.207 --> 00:11:44.887
on his resume, and is unemployable.


00:11:44.927 --> 00:11:46.808
Why unemployable?


00:11:46.848 --> 00:11:50.888
He's 59 and refuses to lie about it.
God, you and my wife.


00:11:50.928 --> 00:11:53.568
Okay... so why do I want him?


00:11:53.608 --> 00:11:56.209
Because we will


00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:58.769
take 15 years off Lou's resume.


00:11:58.809 --> 00:12:00.089
Right, but once he goes
in for the interview,


00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:01.128
they'll just see how old he is, I mean,


00:12:01.129 --> 00:12:02.929
what's the point?


00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:04.168
We don't send him on an interview.


00:12:04.169 --> 00:12:06.850
Lou's what you call a Tracer Bullet.


00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:09.250
A tracer bullet, you know?


00:12:09.291 --> 00:12:10.330
A round that lights up


00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:12.129
so you know where to fire
the rest of the real bullets.


00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:14.329
I know what a tracer bullet is,
I just don't understand...


00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:15.811
..."Relatively Young Lou"


00:12:15.851 --> 00:12:17.530
is a sure-fire bet for
a phone interview, okay?


00:12:17.531 --> 00:12:20.171
But once he's off the line
with a paying customer,


00:12:20.211 --> 00:12:22.811
you bleed "Actually Old Lou"
for information.


00:12:22.851 --> 00:12:24.691
Like, "What projects
are they working on?"


00:12:24.731 --> 00:12:26.853
"What specifically did they ask you?"


00:12:26.892 --> 00:12:28.252
And you give that information


00:12:28.292 --> 00:12:29.931
to your placeable candidates
to prepare them.


00:12:29.932 --> 00:12:32.452
I don't know...


00:12:32.492 --> 00:12:35.092
We're headhunters, Sumner.


00:12:35.132 --> 00:12:37.814
In an economic shit storm.


00:12:37.853 --> 00:12:39.333
Now I can teach you how to count cards,


00:12:39.334 --> 00:12:40.533
but I can't make you do it.


00:12:40.573 --> 00:12:42.293
So you either reach deep inside


00:12:42.333 --> 00:12:44.533
and find that small
dark part of yourself


00:12:44.573 --> 00:12:47.374
that's predatory...
Or there's the door.


00:12:51.694 --> 00:12:53.694
Alright.


00:12:53.735 --> 00:12:57.015
Try giving yourself a desk name,
something tough, visual.


00:12:57.055 --> 00:12:59.975
Watch Wall Street,
